   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Leafy and bushy lichens are healthier and more valuable to scientists than flat, crusty lichens.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Cities should replace their expensive air monitoring stations with volunteer surveys of tree lichens.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Lichens are partnerships between a fungus and an alga that can grow on rock, rooftops and fence posts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Because lichens absorb what is in the air, they can serve as a low-cost, long-term record of air quality.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because lichens absorb what is in the air, they can serve as a low-cost, long-term record of air quality.$q$, $q$The passage moves from how lichens live to why that makes them sensitive and useful as air records, so the first choice covers the whole text. The third choice contradicts paragraph 4, which says lichen surveys "do not replace air monitors."$q$, 'draft', '11940ca5-259d-5c38-9ece-ea1fc10e8679')
