   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Harrowgate's railway station kept a clock that was eleven minutes ahead of the church clock. Shops hung a second clock face, and a few farmers ignored station time for decades.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The railway company forced Harrowgate to change its clocks overnight by passing a national law. Residents had no choice in the matter, and the council vote was simply a formality.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Harrowgate's residents foolishly resisted railway time for years, clinging to the sun even though anyone could see that the railway's system was better. The council finally did the sensible thing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Harrowgate once set its clocks by the sun, but the railway needed one shared time for its timetables. After years of two clocks and some objections, local institutions adopted railway time, and the council made it official.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Harrowgate once set its clocks by the sun, but the railway needed one shared time for its timetables. After years of two clocks and some objections, local institutions adopted railway time, and the council made it official.$q$, $q$The first choice traces the whole sequence without adding judgments. The second uses loaded words such as "foolishly" and "sensible," which make it a biased summary rather than an objective one.$q$, 'draft', 'a0f9180e-714c-52c6-9e4d-582f063048ad')
