   $q$How does the description of the council vote in the final paragraph contribute to the central idea?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By ending with a vote, it suggests that most residents never accepted railway time and were simply outvoted.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"By placing the vote last, it shows that the council was the first group in town to adopt railway time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sequence"},{"text":"By saying the vote only recognized what daily life had decided, it shows that the shared time grew from use rather than from a law.","is_correct":true},{"text":"By showing that the council led the change, it suggests that government action is what made standard time possible.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-relationship"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By saying the vote only recognized what daily life had decided, it shows that the shared time grew from use rather than from a law.$q$, $q$The text says the vote "merely recognized what daily life had already decided," so the law followed the change and supports the idea of a gradual agreement. The second choice reverses that order, since newspapers, schools and the post office had already adopted railway time.$q$, 'draft', 'a0f9180e-714c-52c6-9e4d-582f063048ad')
