   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Conservators often use small cotton swabs and magnifying tools when they clean the surface of an old canvas.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Restoring old paintings by removing yellowed varnish requires careful, reversible methods and difficult judgment about how far to go.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Painters in the past used poor-quality varnish that was designed to change the colors of their work over time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Museums should remove all old varnish from their paintings so that visitors can see the true original colors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Restoring old paintings by removing yellowed varnish requires careful, reversible methods and difficult judgment about how far to go.$q$, $q$The passage covers why varnish changes paintings, how delicately it is removed, the rule of removability and the open question of how far to clean. The third choice ignores paragraph 5, where some conservators argue a warm tone should stay.$q$, 'draft', '5b9a9e3e-ad90-5eb8-8cbb-7f6932e21313')
