   $q$How do the passage's two central ideas, technical skill and judgment, interact over the course of the text?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The passage argues that technical skill matters more than judgment, since a skilled conservator never needs to discuss decisions.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The passage treats judgment as the cause of all past damage and technical skill as the cure that has solved every problem.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"oversimplifies"},{"text":"The passage first shows cleaning as a careful technical process, then reveals that even perfect technique cannot settle how far a painting should be returned.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The passage keeps the two ideas separate, discussing judgment only in the opening and technique only at the end.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The passage first shows cleaning as a careful technical process, then reveals that even perfect technique cannot settle how far a painting should be returned.$q$, $q$Paragraphs 2 through 4 focus on methods and the lessons behind them, and paragraph 5 adds a question "with no simple answer" that requires study and discussion. The final paragraph says decisions follow discussion, so the second choice contradicts the text.$q$, 'draft', '5b9a9e3e-ad90-5eb8-8cbb-7f6932e21313')
