   $q$Which statement best expresses the writer's central claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Westmere should turn off its streetlights at night so that residents can see the stars from every street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Older residents of Westmere remember seeing the pale band of the galaxy from the field behind the school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Westmere should adopt a dark-sky lighting standard because it saves money and protects wildlife without reducing safety.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Night-flying insects gather around lights by the thousands, and many of them never manage to leave.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Westmere should adopt a dark-sky lighting standard because it saves money and protects wildlife without reducing safety.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 states the claim, and paragraphs 3 through 5 give the reasons and answer the safety concern. The writer says the standard "would not mean turning off streetlights," so the second choice contradicts the text.$q$, 'draft', '0f82031e-88f1-5a7f-a969-d3e6f4fc3e6a')
