-- Passage rg11-story-details-inference-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('ec3b98c9-71ed-544e-9759-eba25dd6a1df', 'rg11-story-details-inference-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-story-details-inference'), null,
        '9-12', $q$The Castellano Account$q$, $q$The ledger had come to the Marlow County Historical Society in a box of old hat forms, and nobody had opened it in forty years. Dev Raman's summer job was to type every line into a spreadsheet, which sounded simple until he met the handwriting of Ezra Pruitt, who had run the general store from 1924 to 1938 and apparently believed that vowels were optional.

Most accounts followed a pattern. A family bought flour, lamp oil, nails or thread on credit, and when they settled up, Pruitt wrote "Pd." beside the total, along with the customer's initials and the date. The dates were scattered across every month, the way paydays and harvests would be.

The Castellano account did not fit. From April to November of 1934, the dry year that the society's other records called "the dust summer," the family had bought steadily: flour, seed potatoes, a pair of boot laces, syrup for a child's cough. No payment appeared. Then, on December 31, every one of those entries had been marked "Pd." in darker ink, all at once, with no initials beside them.

Dev turned the ledger toward Mrs. Halvorsen, the society's director. "He let them off," he said. "He just wiped it out."

Mrs. Halvorsen did not answer right away. She turned the page, turned it back, and with the end of a pencil lifted a slip of paper that had been pressed flat in the binding. It was a receipt torn from the pad Pruitt used for deliveries. On the back, in his cramped hand, were four words: R.C. fixed store pump. There was no date.

"Maybe," she said. "Or maybe he was paid in a way that does not show up as money." She laid the slip beside the column. "Type exactly what is on the page, Dev. Put the slip in a note. Whoever reads this later can argue about it."

Dev typed "Pd." eleven times. Then, in the note field, he typed the four words and nothing else, though it took him a while.$q$, 'draft')
