   $q$What does the brother's tying and untying his shoes, "a job he could finish," suggest about him?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He is eager to leave and is getting ready to walk out the door.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-reading"},{"text":"He is unsettled by the move and wants something he can control.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He is too young to have learned how to tie his shoes properly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"He refuses to help because he is angry at his mother.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He is unsettled by the move and wants something he can control.$q$, $q$Repeating a small task "he could finish" while the family dismantles their home suggests he is seeking control in an unsettling moment. Nothing shows anger at his mother, and the repetition is not a sign that he cannot tie shoes.$q$, 'draft', '2cf481d5-3cf4-5436-a134-7e4cbc0c6080')
