   $q$What do the lines "He was a kind man. He had waited a week." suggest about the speaker's attitude toward the landlord?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker suspects he is pretending to be kind.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The speaker does not blame him and knows he gave them extra time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The speaker barely knows him and has no opinion of him.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-evidence"},{"text":"The speaker blames him for forcing the family to move out.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker does not blame him and knows he gave them extra time.$q$, $q$Calling him "kind" and noting that he "waited a week" shows the speaker sees the painting as fair, not cruel. Nothing in the poem says he forced the family out.$q$, 'draft', '2cf481d5-3cf4-5436-a134-7e4cbc0c6080')
