   $q$Which statement is suggested by the story but never directly confirmed?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The fox uses the acorns to repair and improve the canyon trail.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The price of an echo at the booth is one acorn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Brisk walked past the white line before shouting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The echo returns each traveler's words three times.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The fox uses the acorns to repair and improve the canyon trail.$q$, $q$The narrator says only that "Someone" stretched the rope and does not name who fixed the trail, so the link to the fox is an inference Brisk and the reader make. The three echoes, the white line and the price are all stated directly.$q$, 'draft', '6ca79473-7f0b-539b-8f69-1fa6e082c138')
