   $q$How does paragraph 4, beginning "This simple rule has a weakness, however," function in the structure?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It returns to the opening claim that people cannot stop making mistakes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-paragraphs"},{"text":"It repeats the example from paragraph 3 with a different card number.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-shift"},{"text":"It shows that check digits never catch any real typing mistakes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"It signals a turn to a limitation of the example, which leads into how real systems improve on it.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It signals a turn to a limitation of the example, which leads into how real systems improve on it.$q$, $q$"However" marks a shift from success to a weakness (swapped digits), and the paragraph then explains the more elaborate rules real systems use. It says only the simple rule misses swaps, not that check digits never work.$q$, 'draft', 'f0a349e6-6e78-55ad-ac86-6916d81097b2')
