  ('f439e2ee-1436-53e9-a60d-f2599118bc96', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-theme-summary'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How does the aunt's answer in the second stanza develop the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It proves that the aunt believes her measurements will stop the ice from retreating.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It explains the scientific method for calculating how fast a glacier melts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It shows that she is annoyed by the speaker's question and refuses to answer it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"By handing over the tape and saying the job is holding steady, she shows that the meaning lies in the act of witnessing itself.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By handing over the tape and saying the job is holding steady, she shows that the meaning lies in the act of witnessing itself.$q$, $q$Instead of explaining, she makes the speaker take part, suggesting that steady attention is the point. She does not claim to stop the retreat; the speaker's question admits she "could not stop" it.$q$, 'draft', '5014dedd-4788-5a9b-815f-3c11a732119c')
