   $q$How does the final log entry show the themes of achievement and connection interacting?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The entry shows Priya is embarrassed by her slow time and wants to hide it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Priya writes the time in large letters, showing achievement still matters most to her.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"Priya writes only the sentence, showing she no longer cares about running times.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She records both the time and the shared mile, showing she now values connection alongside achievement.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She records both the time and the shared mile, showing she now values connection alongside achievement.$q$, $q$Priya writes the time and then, beneath it, "Ran the last mile with someone," so both kinds of value sit together on the page. She does not drop the time, which rules out the choice saying she wrote only the sentence.$q$, 'draft', '84cd6bc4-cabe-557e-b99a-2929b048090e')
