   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A volunteer scanning mill records finds a weaver's margin notes, persuades the archivist to scan them, and credits the weaver in the catalog.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A bored volunteer scans letters about cotton prices, a boiler, and a railroad dispute.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A volunteer discovers the full name of the weaver E.M. and finds the weaver's living family.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"A volunteer heroically saves the most important papers in the county from being lost forever.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A volunteer scanning mill records finds a weaver's margin notes, persuades the archivist to scan them, and credits the weaver in the catalog.$q$, $q$The correct choice includes the discovery, the decision, and the catalog entry with no judgment. "Heroically" and "most important" are opinions, and the weaver's identity stays unknown.$q$, 'draft', 'd3f6bc26-2ac5-5558-9e14-0c71661a3691')
