   $q$Which statement best expresses a central theme of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Bridges are dangerous structures that people should avoid crossing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Work that prevents problems has great value even when almost no one notices it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Working at night is more difficult than working during the day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Children should always choose the same careers as their parents.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Work that prevents problems has great value even when almost no one notices it.$q$, $q$The speaker says "some work is measured by what never happens," pointing to the hidden value of the father's job. The poem shows bridges as trusted, not dangerous, because of his work.$q$, 'draft', '391883cd-e59b-59f4-96ca-3600b90501f6')
