  ('22789b90-8aeb-56e3-b581-958fac523ac9', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The prefix syn- means "together," chron means "time," and the suffix -ize means "to make." What did the officers do when they "synchronized" the chronometer with a trusted clock?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They set it so that both clocks showed exactly the same time","is_correct":true},{"text":"They compared it to the trusted clock only after the voyage","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sequence"},{"text":"They replaced it with the trusted clock for the whole voyage","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They took it apart and rebuilt it with the trusted clock's parts","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They set it so that both clocks showed exactly the same time$q$, $q$To synchronize is to make two things match in time, and the officers did this "before departure" so they could check the drift later. Comparing the clocks after the voyage is a separate step the passage describes, not the meaning of synchronized.$q$, 'draft', 'a20ce9b9-aa4e-5b16-b827-5dbdd987f7a5')
