   $q$Why is the Calder Bay attendance figure weak support for the claim that allowing photography draws visitors?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author does not say how many visitors Harwick receives each year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-gap"},{"text":"The figure comes from a museum that never allowed any photography at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"An 18 percent rise is too small to matter for any museum's budget.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A new sculpture wing opened the same year and could explain the rise.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A new sculpture wing opened the same year and could explain the rise.$q$, $q$The author admits Calder Bay "opened its new sculpture wing" that same year, so the attendance rise may have another cause. Harwick's own attendance is not needed to judge whether the Calder Bay evidence shows cause.$q$, 'draft', '3ad6a6b9-6300-5439-8fed-2bc15355f38a')
