  ('c49036fc-9a8f-56e1-8860-ffb8d809fb54', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-argument-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Why does the assumption in the cost paragraph matter to the author's reasoning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that printed textbooks also need repairs every year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It proves that tablets will last longer than printed books.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-text"},{"text":"It explains why the digital editions can be updated quickly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-paragraphs"},{"text":"If tablets need repairs, the claimed savings could shrink or vanish.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$If tablets need repairs, the claimed savings could shrink or vanish.$q$, $q$The savings figure holds only if "each tablet lasts the full five years without repair," so any repair costs would cut into it. The author states this as an assumption, so it proves nothing about how long tablets actually last.$q$, 'draft', 'f703690a-a9cb-5303-a60e-c37844202b2b')
