   $q$What conclusion did the Westmere researchers draw from their study?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Students prefer nine-inch plates to eleven-inch plates.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Dining halls should weigh every plate at the end of each meal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mistakes-method-for-claim"},{"text":"Smaller plates help students lose weight over a semester.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"Smaller plates limit first servings and so reduce food waste.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Smaller plates limit first servings and so reduce food waste.$q$, $q$The researchers reasoned that "a smaller plate ... limits the first serving and therefore limits waste." The passage stresses that the study did not measure weight or health.$q$, 'draft', '09d51f2c-d3a8-5f97-bdbb-771951c33afd')
