insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('4edd66d6-6d04-5b9f-bb6a-423afcb39df1', 'rg12-argument-evidence-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-argument-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$A Trail Along the Old Spur Line$q$, $q$For eleven years, the abandoned Corwin rail spur has cut a weedy, three-mile strip through the middle of our county, from the edge of Hallam to the village of Ashby Mills. The county commission should buy the corridor from the railroad and turn it into a paved trail for walking and cycling.

A trail would give residents a safe, level place to exercise. Hallam has no sidewalk along Route 9, and many students who live within a mile of Ashby Mills High School are driven to school because walking along the highway shoulder is too dangerous. A trail would connect their neighborhoods directly to the campus.

A trail would also bring business. Since the Gresham Valley trail opened four years ago, three new cafes have opened along its route. Our own small towns could see the same kind of growth.

Some homeowners whose yards back onto the corridor worry about strangers passing close to their windows. The plan I support sets aside part of the budget for fences and tall plantings wherever a neighbor requests them, and it closes the trail from dusk to dawn.

The public has spoken, too. More than two thousand residents have signed a petition supporting the trail, and that level of support should settle the question for the commission.

The choice before us is simple. Either the county builds this trail now, or the corridor will remain a dumping ground for old tires and broken furniture forever. I urge the commission to choose the trail.$q$, 'draft')
