   $q$What is the effect of the sentence "The coxswain is their eyes, and in the final two hundred meters ... the coxswain is often their will as well"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It admits that the coxswain becomes less important as the boat gets closer to the finish line.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"},{"text":"It introduces a new topic, the training schedule rowers follow in the weeks before a race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It moves from the coxswain's physical role to a psychological one, raising the stakes of the argument.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It suggests that rowers lose their eyesight and their courage during the last part of a race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It moves from the coxswain's physical role to a psychological one, raising the stakes of the argument.$q$, $q$The parallel phrasing climbs from "eyes" (seeing for the crew) to "will" (keeping them going), so the coxswain's importance grows at the moment it matters most. The sentence makes the coxswain more important near the finish, not less.$q$, 'draft', 'e91a5a3c-7b4a-5798-8092-5bb46737a70d')
