   $q$The speaker says of the coach only, "Coach never mentioned it. That was worse." How does this brief introduction of the coach shape the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The coach's silence sets up a later scene in which the coach praises the clean handoff.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The coach's silence shows that the dropped baton did not matter to the team's results.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The coach's silence suggests the coach blamed Desmond rather than the speaker for the drop.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The coach's silence leaves the failure unresolved, so the speaker must settle it alone in the present race.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The coach's silence leaves the failure unresolved, so the speaker must settle it alone in the present race.$q$, $q$Because no one ever addressed the mistake, the speaker carries it privately into this race, which is why the handoff matters so much. "That was worse" shows the silence did matter, and the coach never reappears.$q$, 'draft', '03e6d0f6-e71c-5fe6-899b-f266f515aef5')
