   $q$How does the laundromat setting shape the rules of the chess club?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Games are played in silence so that customers can do their laundry in peace.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Games are timed by digital clocks that Mr. Baptiste keeps behind the counter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Games are timed by dryer loads, so each one ends when a buzzer sounds.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Games are limited to members who bring their own laundry to the tables.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Games are timed by dryer loads, so each one ends when a buzzer sounds.$q$, $q$The club "used the dryers to keep time," and the game ends "when the buzzer sounded." The club has "no clocks," and the room is loud, not silent.$q$, 'draft', 'abf12121-e77a-5ab8-8b6e-30491211e8f8')
