   $q$According to the story, why does Wen lose her first four games?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The noise of the machines and the running toddler keep her from seeing the board.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Her habit of planning long attacks clashes with games that a buzzer can cut short.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Mr. Baptiste judges the positions unfairly because he does not play chess himself.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Her opponents at the laundromat are much stronger than the players she knew at school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Her habit of planning long attacks clashes with games that a buzzer can cut short.$q$, $q$She lost "not because her opponents were stronger but because she kept planning long attacks that the buzzer cut off halfway." The noise is described, but the text names the attacks as the cause.$q$, 'draft', 'abf12121-e77a-5ab8-8b6e-30491211e8f8')
