  ('e29c1360-1586-5d4b-a941-15026112b81e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-character-setting-plot'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Why does pulling the damp quilt from the dryer work as the turning point of the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that Mrs. Odunsi has forgotten the club rules after so many years of playing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It removes the only timer, so Wen can no longer plan around a known ending and must change how she plays.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It distracts Wen, who makes a careless move and loses her careful attack on the king's side.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It ends the game early, so Mr. Baptiste declares Mrs. Odunsi the winner on the spot.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It removes the only timer, so Wen can no longer plan around a known ending and must change how she plays.$q$, $q$With no buzzer coming, Wen "had no idea how long she had," so she stops chasing a planned attack and plays the position. The game continues and Wen wins, so it does not end early.$q$, 'draft', 'abf12121-e77a-5ab8-8b6e-30491211e8f8')
