   $q$What role does the river play in the plot of the fable?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Its slow change of course opens a gap between the map and reality, creating the central conflict.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Its pine forests attract travelers who pay Orsolya to draw more maps.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Its sudden flood destroys the village hall and the map hanging inside it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Its steady, unchanging path proves that Orsolya's map was perfectly made.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Its slow change of course opens a gap between the map and reality, creating the central conflict.$q$, $q$The river "leaned a little farther east" each spring, so the ford on the map became dangerous. There is no sudden flood, and the map survives in a chest.$q$, 'draft', 'a0b3406e-1f54-5269-ae36-e6c1b5421933')
