   $q$How do the points of view of the two texts differ?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Text 1 follows the person being photographed, while Text 2 is spoken by a painter addressing the camera directly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Both texts are told by the same painter, first in prose and then again in verse.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"Text 1 is told by the grandmother looking back, while Text 2 is spoken by a crowd of townspeople.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Text 1 is narrated by the camera operator, while Text 2 is spoken by the young woman in the portrait.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Text 1 follows the person being photographed, while Text 2 is spoken by a painter addressing the camera directly.$q$, $q$Text 1 stays close to Hana's thoughts and disappointment, and Text 2 uses "I" for a painter who speaks to "you," the "honest box of glass and light." No narrator in Text 1 is the operator.$q$, 'draft', 'f37a730c-34b2-54aa-a620-b762b8824e8f')
