   $q$How does each text present the flight itself?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both texts describe the flight from the aviator's seat, high above the fairground.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The poem offers only fragments seen between tasks, while the story follows the takeoff closely from start to finish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"Neither text describes the flight, since both focus only on what happens afterward.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The poem follows the takeoff closely from start to finish, while the story offers only fragments seen by a busy worker.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The poem follows the takeoff closely from start to finish, while the story offers only fragments seen by a busy worker.$q$, $q$The poem moves through the coughing, rolling and rising in order, but Clementine "caught the flight in pieces" while pouring and making change. The aviator's view is reported only in his later words.$q$, 'draft', 'a97e75f1-088a-5fef-b542-64f75efb5484')
