   $q$How do the forms of the two texts shape their treatment of the topic?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both texts use rhyming stanzas to give the night sky a playful, singsong tone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-form"},{"text":"Both texts are written as scientific reports that measure the brightness of the sky.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-form"},{"text":"Text 1 uses a list from one spot to take stock of what remains, while Text 2 uses a journey to show the loss.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"Text 1 uses a journey from dark to bright to show the loss, while Text 2 uses a list from one spot to take stock of what remains.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Text 1 uses a journey from dark to bright to show the loss, while Text 2 uses a list from one spot to take stock of what remains.$q$, $q$Text 1 tracks the stars fading "mile by mile" on the drive home, while the poem stays on a fire escape and lists a planet, jets, a satellite and the moon. The poem does not rhyme, so the stanza choice is wrong.$q$, 'draft', '02105ba7-b9f2-5a4c-a9c7-a6649a325864')
